<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers 7.5 bln levs 3-mth T-bills Oct 14.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers 7.5 bln levs 3-mth T-bills Oct 14.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer 7.5 billion levs of three-month floater coupon T-bills at an auction on Monday, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue will be offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry, a BNB statement said.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 300 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3019796021</p>
<p> Par value	    7.5 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	 October 14, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   October 16, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	January 15, 1997</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
